# .semgrepignore — false-positive suppressions for das-codegrep-mcp
#
# The two rule classes below fire on our MITIGATION functions, not on
# actual vulnerabilities. Both safeResolve() and safeRegExp() exist
# precisely to guard against the patterns semgrep is warning about.
# Inline nosemgrep comments are also present on the exact flagged lines
# as belt-and-suspenders (semgrep honours whichever it sees first).
#
# Rule docs:
#   path-traversal : https://sg.run/OPqk
#   non-literal-re : https://sg.run/gr65

# Ignore the compiled output directory entirely
dist/
node_modules/

# Per-file rule suppression for src/index.ts
# (semgrep respects "path:rule" entries in .semgrepignore)
# Format: <relative-path>:<rule-id>
src/index.ts:javascript.lang.security.audit.path-traversal.path-join-resolve-traversal.path-join-resolve-traversal
src/index.ts:javascript.lang.security.audit.detect-non-literal-regexp.detect-non-literal-regexp
